    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0117" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.0021/131</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1375</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instructions Nos.
                    322 and 323 of April 4, 1918, regarding the abrogation of the treaties concluded
                    by the Government of the United States and the Government of the Netherlands on
                    January 19, 1839, and May 23, 1878, respectively, which were received by me on
                    the 10th of May, 1918, I have the honor to enclose herewith copies of my
                        notes<anchor n="1" xml:id="d5-f1"/> of the latter date to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs in which I carried out your instructions to denounce these
                    treaties, and of the reply of the Minister for Foreign Affairs—together with a
                    translation—of June 3, 1918. The Minister for Foreign Affairs in his reply takes
                    note of the statement in my communications to him to the effect that the two
                    treaties in question will terminate on May 10, 1919.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. W. Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d5-a1.xml" xpointer="d5-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d5-f1" n="1" xml:id="d5-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Notes are identical with paragraphs 2 to 5 of instruction No. 322,
                    and paragraphs 2 and 3 of instruction No. 323, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg3">pp. 3</ref>–<ref target="#pg5">5</ref>, with the
                    date, May 10, 1919, inserted in the blank spaces in the instructions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
